{
  "name": "regex-modifier-scope-fold-table",
  "description": "Modifier groups, the case-fold table and escaped letters follow Dart's RegExp (ECMAScript). A modifier group changes `i` for its own contents only: `(?-i:s)` with `gi` on \"sS\" gives \"#S\" (the group turns `i` off), `(?i:s)` with `g` on \"\u017fsS\" gives \"\u017f##\" (the group turns it on, and without `u` the long s U+017F still matches no ASCII letter), and `a(?i:b)c` with `g` on \"aBc ABc aBC\" gives \"# ABc aBC\" (only the b ignores case). Without `u`, `i` compares each character's uppercase and keeps a character whose uppercase is not one character: the Angstrom sign U+212B is its own uppercase while U+00E5 and U+00C5 share U+00C5, so U+212B on \"\u212b\u00e5\u00c5\" gives \"#\u00e5\u00c5\"; the sharp s U+00DF (uppercase \"SS\") matches neither \"ss\" nor the capital sharp s U+1E9E, \"\u00df ss \u1e9e\" gives \"# ss \u1e9e\"; `ff` does not match the ligature U+FB00 (uppercase \"FF\"), \"\ufb00 ff\" gives \"\ufb00 #\"; and `[^^a]` excludes the caret and both cases of a, \"^aAfF\" gives \"^aA##\". With `giu` simple case folding applies: U+212B, U+00E5 and U+00C5 all fold to U+00E5 (\"###\") and U+1E9E folds to U+00DF (\"# ss #\"). An escaped letter folds as the letter itself, with `gi`: `\\x73` is s (\"s S \u017f\" gives \"# # \u017f\"), `\\u017f` matches only the long s (\"s S #\") and `\\u0130` only the dotted capital I (\"iI\u0130\u0131\" gives \"iI#\u0131\"). With `gu`, `\\u{73}` is s (\"sS\" gives \"#S\") and `\\u{1F600}` is one code point, one match per emoji (\"\ud83d\ude00a\ud83d\ude00\" gives \"#a#\"). Every replace-mode regex puts \"#\" for each match. Every input reads page state, so the engine keeps the Values unresolved with `watches` and the client resolves them.",
